      "description": "Bret Victor’s October 2011 interactive essay uses a simple car-control simulation to show how designers can move between a particular run and broader views of possible behaviour. Time and steering parameters can be varied; trajectories expose patterns that are difficult to see during real-time playback. Moving back to a concrete case tests what an abstract picture hides. The essay offers a practical approach to exploring a system when theory is insufficient to predict the consequences of design decisions.",
