      "description": "Yu Zheng and colleagues report a method that turns learned network-attack strategies into interpretable formulas for assessing resilience. Their account considers both network structure and the dynamical states imposed on it, including the association between node degree and state. The method aims to identify components whose removal can cause a network to fail. The Nature Communications abstract is the basis of this description: the reported performance improvements belong to the authors’ evaluated settings, and do not establish a general measure for every social or organisational use of resilience.",
